At what situations TS serves best?
a) A function accepts 2 numbers. → In the regular JS code, once a function accepts the number, then you check the type of these values to make sure that these are actual numbers. In TS you don't have to explicitly check that. So extra lines of code that you don't have to write.
b) A function returns a string. → Using TS you are absolutely sure that a function will always return the correct data type. When you're working with a team, TS makes life a lot easier.

Syntax:
